  "id": "passive-aggressive-personality-disorder",
  "term": "passive-aggressive personality disorder",
  "definition": "Passive-aggressive personality disorder is a personality disorder in which a person pushes back against expected social or work responsibilities in indirect rather than open ways. Frustration with authority or with what others want may show up through covert noncooperation, such as delaying, obstructing, being stubborn, seeming forgetful, or working inefficiently on purpose.",
